\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}
\PYG{+w}{  }\PYG{n+nt}{\PYGZdq{}action\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{:}\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}delegate\PYGZus{}task\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}
\PYG{+w}{  }\PYG{n+nt}{\PYGZdq{}reasoning\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{:}\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}Previous attempts have correctly identified the target set as}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{  the Qing dynasty jade \PYGZsq{}Twelve animals of the Chinese zodiac\PYGZsq{} (Accession 02.18.730a–l),}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{  which was featured in the 2015 exhibition \PYGZsq{}Celebrating the Year of the Ram\PYGZsq{}.}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{  However, they failed to produce a final count of figures with visible hands.}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{  I will delegate a task to perform a definitive count by examining the high\PYGZhy{}resolution images}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{  or detailed descriptions of each of the twelve figures (a through l).\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}
\PYG{+w}{  }\PYG{n+nt}{\PYGZdq{}params\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{:}\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{p}{\PYGZob{}}
\PYG{+w}{    }\PYG{n+nt}{\PYGZdq{}task\PYGZus{}instruction\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{:}\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{    1. Access the Metropolitan Museum\PYGZsq{}s collection page for accession number 02.18.730}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{    (Object ID 42102) and its sub\PYGZhy{}items (02.18.730a through 02.18.730l).}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{    \PYGZbs{}n2. For each of the twelve figures in this set, determine if a hand}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{    (fingers, hand structure, or paws clearly acting as hands) is visible outside of the robe sleeves.}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{    Often these figures are holding objects like fans, scrolls, or brushes, which makes the hand visible.}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{    \PYGZbs{}n3. Count the total number of figures out of the twelve that have at least one hand visible.}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{    \PYGZbs{}n4. Provide the final integer count as the answer.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}
\PYG{+w}{    }\PYG{n+nt}{\PYGZdq{}context\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{:}\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}The 2015 Met exhibition is \PYGZsq{}Celebrating the Year of the Ram\PYGZsq{}.}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{    The relevant set of \PYGZsq{}twelve animals\PYGZsq{} is 02.18.730a–l. Use high\PYGZhy{}resolution images like DT5058.jpg}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{    (found on the Met website)}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{    or individual item photos to verify the visibility of hands for each figure}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{    (Rat, Ox, Tiger, Rabbit, Dragon, Snake, Horse, Ram, Monkey, Rooster, Dog, Pig).}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{    Note that \PYGZsq{}visible\PYGZsq{} means the hand is not completely tucked into a sleeve.\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{,}
\PYG{+w}{    }\PYG{n+nt}{\PYGZdq{}model\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{p}{:}\PYG{+w}{ }\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}model\PYGZus{}1\PYGZdq{}}
